            <li>You must have a lawful basis or the contact's permission before adding their personal information or causing them to receive alerts.</li>
            <li>You are responsible for keeping contact details current and testing your configuration in a safe, non-emergency setting.</li>
            <li>You must not trigger false, deceptive, harassing or unlawful alerts.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>6. Google Drive and SOS recordings</h2>
          <p>Connecting Google Drive is optional. If connected, completing an SOS recording automatically starts an upload through our server to your Drive using the <code>drive.file</code> permission. The server relays the recording and does not retain a local video copy. Panic Button makes the resulting Drive file viewable by anyone with its link so an emergency contact can watch it from the alert page. Anyone who obtains that link may view or forward it.</p>
          <p>You control files stored in your Drive and may revoke Panic Button's Google authorization at any time. Disconnecting or deleting your Panic Button account does not automatically delete files already uploaded to Drive. See our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for complete data-handling details.</p>

          <h2>7. Acceptable use</h2>
